  m_Name: Highpressure_turbine_shaft
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  partName: High Pressure Turbine Shaft
  description: The High Pressure Turbine Shaft is a thin, flat, tiny part located
    at the middle-center of the engine, constructed from high-pressure shaft material.
    It is vital for transmitting power from the high-pressure turbine to the engine's
    gearbox, driving the engine's accessories. A notable feature of this shaft is
    its ability to withstand extremely high pressures and stresses while maintaining
    rotational stability.
  audioExplanation: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 6e0b49cfbb1a17d4585cab62254774c0, type: 3}
